


The estream_put_text function "estream_put_text.h"

            The estream_put_text function is intended to
            support the sending of embedded diagnostic and
            error messages to the standard error stream.
              The estream_put_text function indirectly sends
            the words of the string specified by #0 to the
            standard error stream. Leading and trailing
            spaces are ignored. Words are separated by
            spaces; each internal contiguous sequence of
            spaces separating the words of the string
            results in a word separator being sent to the
            standard error stream.
